WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:03.260 --> 00:00:08.260
Singapore is one of the world's
biggest oil-trading centers

00:00:08.350 --> 00:00:13.350
and Hin Leong is a homegrown
oil trader in Singapore.

00:00:13.910 --> 00:00:17.250
Hin Leong has also always
been very secretive.

00:00:17.250 --> 00:00:20.130
It's held by its founder Oon Kuin Lim,

00:00:20.130 --> 00:00:22.980
his son and his daughter.

00:00:22.980 --> 00:00:25.590
So very little is actually
known about Hin Leong.

00:00:25.590 --> 00:00:27.170
And we've also got this fallout

00:00:27.170 --> 00:00:30.560
from the Singapore oil trader, Hin Leong.

00:00:30.560 --> 00:00:32.410
Investigations started in April

00:00:32.410 --> 00:00:35.280
after Hin Leong filed for
bankruptcy protection.

00:00:35.280 --> 00:00:37.660
It was revealed that Lim
had asked the company

00:00:37.660 --> 00:00:40.540
to hide nearly a billion dollars in losses

00:00:40.540 --> 00:00:44.260
from speculating oil
futures over the years.

00:00:44.260 --> 00:00:49.130
So it all started when
we heard that major banks

00:00:49.130 --> 00:00:52.760
were pulling financing from
the oil trader Hin Leong.

00:00:52.760 --> 00:00:56.500
And at first, we were shocked
to hear this information.

00:00:56.500 --> 00:00:58.060
Hin Leong is such a big name

00:00:58.060 --> 00:01:00.660
in the Asian oil-trading industry

00:01:00.660 --> 00:01:03.520
and why were the banks
unwilling to finance

00:01:03.520 --> 00:01:05.003
Hin Leong any further.

00:01:06.050 --> 00:01:09.520
All the answers only
came to us much later.

00:01:17.840 --> 00:01:19.290
My name is Alfred Cang.

00:01:19.290 --> 00:01:21.930
I'm a senior reporter with Bloomberg News.

00:01:21.930 --> 00:01:23.390
I'm Serene Cheong.

00:01:23.390 --> 00:01:25.220
I'm a reporter at Bloomberg.

00:01:25.220 --> 00:01:28.620
Serene and I and other
colleagues in Singapore office

00:01:28.620 --> 00:01:32.090
wrote the story about the
collapse of Hin Leong,

00:01:32.090 --> 00:01:36.237
one of the biggest independent
oil traders in the world.

00:01:36.237 --> 00:01:38.750
So Hin Leong is in the business

00:01:38.750 --> 00:01:41.200
of what we call bunkering,

00:01:41.200 --> 00:01:44.660
which is to supply shipping
fuel to all the vessels

00:01:44.660 --> 00:01:48.210
that come into the Singapore
ports for refueling.

00:01:48.210 --> 00:01:53.200
It's actually owned and
founded by Lim Oon Kuin,

00:01:53.200 --> 00:01:55.013
also known as OK Lim.

00:01:55.870 --> 00:01:58.820
OK Lim was born in
Fujian province of China.

00:01:58.820 --> 00:02:02.620
He immigrated to Singapore in 1950s.

00:02:02.620 --> 00:02:07.440
From the associates who've
known OK Lim for decades,

00:02:07.440 --> 00:02:11.460
OK Lim was described as a low-key, humble,

00:02:11.460 --> 00:02:13.420
aggressive oil trader

00:02:13.420 --> 00:02:16.550
and always honest to his origin.

00:02:16.550 --> 00:02:21.550
OK Lim likes dining in a
Singapore-based chain restaurant

00:02:21.880 --> 00:02:24.970
which serves his homeland food.

00:02:24.970 --> 00:02:28.373
He is also known as a keen poker player.

00:02:30.140 --> 00:02:34.530
He started off as a
one-man, one-truck business.

00:02:34.530 --> 00:02:38.350
He would buy fuel from oil majors,

00:02:38.350 --> 00:02:41.380
parcel it up into smaller volumes

00:02:41.380 --> 00:02:45.440
and resell it to taxi
companies, to bus companies

00:02:45.440 --> 00:02:47.410
as well as to fishing boats.

00:02:47.410 --> 00:02:50.360
OK Lim's business later developed

00:02:50.360 --> 00:02:53.990
to involve a lot more of these tank trucks

00:02:53.990 --> 00:02:57.910
and later on, it also developed to include

00:02:57.910 --> 00:03:00.490
an entire fleet of vessels

00:03:00.490 --> 00:03:04.210
that will actually work as
an integrated supply system

00:03:04.210 --> 00:03:09.210
to allow him to buy, float
and sell fuel to customers

00:03:10.220 --> 00:03:11.870
around the region.

00:03:11.870 --> 00:03:13.850
Hin Leong actually developed

00:03:13.850 --> 00:03:17.060
alongside the Singapore oil trading hub.

00:03:17.060 --> 00:03:20.040
And as more and more
boats came to Singapore

00:03:20.040 --> 00:03:22.040
to dock and refuel,

00:03:22.040 --> 00:03:24.770
Hin Leong grew because
it was opportunistically

00:03:24.770 --> 00:03:26.620
at the right place at the right time.

00:03:31.410 --> 00:03:34.310
So different from stock-market trading,

00:03:34.310 --> 00:03:38.450
where information are
basically available publicly,

00:03:38.450 --> 00:03:42.090
oil traders in the world
rely on the information

00:03:42.090 --> 00:03:47.090
private to a small group and
find the business opportunity.

00:03:47.780 --> 00:03:49.410
Our understanding of OK Lim

00:03:49.410 --> 00:03:54.080
is that he is a trader with
a very big appetite for risk.

00:03:54.080 --> 00:03:57.040
He's also one that
thrives in the very opaque

00:03:57.040 --> 00:04:00.780
and secretive market
of oil trading in Asia.

00:04:00.780 --> 00:04:05.340
So for example, at any one
point in the Asian market,

00:04:05.340 --> 00:04:07.630
no one trader would actually know

00:04:07.630 --> 00:04:11.250
exactly how much supply
and how much demand

00:04:11.250 --> 00:04:13.490
there is at any given time.

00:04:13.490 --> 00:04:16.970
OK Lim would reach deep into his resources

00:04:16.970 --> 00:04:21.970
and leverage on his relationships
with his counterparts

00:04:22.400 --> 00:04:24.920
to actually figure out
what exactly was happening

00:04:24.920 --> 00:04:26.030
in the market

00:04:26.030 --> 00:04:29.790
and therefore to make bold
decisions to dominate the market

00:04:29.790 --> 00:04:33.910
and create a trading position
that's beneficial for himself.

00:04:33.910 --> 00:04:37.940
Once they purchased
enough physical stockpiles

00:04:37.940 --> 00:04:38.940
in the market

00:04:38.940 --> 00:04:43.410
and created disruptions

00:04:43.410 --> 00:04:47.340
in a certain time of
period and a certain area,

00:04:47.340 --> 00:04:51.730
it did squeeze the market
and push the prices higher.

00:04:51.730 --> 00:04:55.620
In that case, Hin Leong
and OK Lim can always sell

00:04:55.620 --> 00:04:59.070
the inventories and sell
the products to end users

00:04:59.070 --> 00:05:02.160
or other merchants for profit.

00:05:02.160 --> 00:05:07.160
This strategy was one of
the source of his success

00:05:07.290 --> 00:05:09.523
for decades but not for this time.

00:05:16.610 --> 00:05:20.120
In April of 2020, my colleague and I

00:05:20.120 --> 00:05:24.640
had heard that banks were pulling
financing and credit lines

00:05:24.640 --> 00:05:26.110
away from Hin Leong.

00:05:26.110 --> 00:05:29.760
And as we know, financing,
credit lines and liquidity

00:05:29.760 --> 00:05:31.540
are the lifeblood of trading.

00:05:31.540 --> 00:05:34.710
So we knew that something big was brewing,

00:05:34.710 --> 00:05:36.810
but we just didn't know what it was yet.

00:05:36.810 --> 00:05:38.790
And it was only in the coming weeks

00:05:38.790 --> 00:05:41.713
that more information and
the answers were unveiled.

00:05:43.570 --> 00:05:47.140
Covid-19 brought the global
economy to a screeching halt

00:05:47.140 --> 00:05:49.840
and one industry hit
particularly hard was oil.

00:05:49.840 --> 00:05:53.380
In the USA, the price of oil
has collapsed to a record low

00:05:53.380 --> 00:05:56.570
as demand dries up and storage runs out.

00:05:56.570 --> 00:05:59.290
The price of a barrel of
West Texas Intermediate,

00:05:59.290 --> 00:06:01.490
which is the benchmark for U.S. oil,

00:06:01.490 --> 00:06:05.260
today traded as low as -$40 a barrel.

00:06:05.260 --> 00:06:07.930
It's the first time the
price has turned negative

00:06:07.930 --> 00:06:08.780
in history.

00:06:08.780 --> 00:06:10.950
According to the documents we've seen,

00:06:10.950 --> 00:06:14.840
Hin Leong barely hedged
the physical stockpiles

00:06:14.840 --> 00:06:15.890
it's purchased.

00:06:15.890 --> 00:06:18.930
So all of its physical stockpiles

00:06:18.930 --> 00:06:23.600
are purely exposed to
the market fluctuations.

00:06:23.600 --> 00:06:26.830
Because the oil benchmark prices

00:06:26.830 --> 00:06:30.047
slumped on coronavirus
outbreaks in the world.

00:06:30.047 --> 00:06:34.250
The value of physical
stockpiles of Hin Leong reduced.

00:06:34.250 --> 00:06:38.400
We know from our sources that
OK Lim made opposition bets

00:06:38.400 --> 00:06:41.420
on the oil prices because he believed

00:06:41.420 --> 00:06:45.790
China will soon put the
coronavirus in control

00:06:45.790 --> 00:06:48.740
and the demand will recover very quickly.

00:06:48.740 --> 00:06:53.490
So OK Lim was right in the
first half of his prediction.

00:06:53.490 --> 00:06:58.180
China did contain the
outbreaks of coronavirus,

00:06:58.180 --> 00:07:01.600
but what OK Lim didn't see is

00:07:01.600 --> 00:07:04.650
the outbreak turn into a pandemic

00:07:04.650 --> 00:07:07.643
and create larger demand destructions.

00:07:09.760 --> 00:07:13.080
And banks start coming after him,

00:07:13.080 --> 00:07:16.900
asking him to repay the unpaid debts.

00:07:16.900 --> 00:07:20.390
Dozens of commercial and
investment banks in Singapore

00:07:20.390 --> 00:07:25.390
have a combined exposure of
US$3.5 billion to Hin Leong,

00:07:26.580 --> 00:07:31.580
of which HSBC had the biggest
exposure of $600 million.

00:07:32.030 --> 00:07:35.570
And other banks, such as DBS and ABN,

00:07:35.570 --> 00:07:39.503
had more than $200 million
exposure to Hin Leong.

00:07:41.650 --> 00:07:43.710
So from speaking to our sources

00:07:43.710 --> 00:07:46.320
and from documents that we obtained,

00:07:46.320 --> 00:07:51.150
we came to realize that Hin
Leong had actually not made

00:07:51.150 --> 00:07:54.140
any profits for a couple of years

00:07:54.140 --> 00:07:58.200
and that some of the oil
that Hin Leong had used

00:07:58.200 --> 00:08:01.840
for collaterals were
actually already resold

00:08:01.840 --> 00:08:03.520
to other customers.

00:08:03.520 --> 00:08:08.520
It was shocking to see that
the company had actually hid

00:08:09.360 --> 00:08:11.743
$800 million in losses.

00:08:13.000 --> 00:08:15.290
The growth model of Singapore,

00:08:15.290 --> 00:08:19.320
the Southeast Asia and
China has been changed

00:08:19.320 --> 00:08:20.670
through these years.

00:08:20.670 --> 00:08:23.780
And that could be part of the reason

00:08:23.780 --> 00:08:27.370
why Hin Leong didn't make any profits.

00:08:27.370 --> 00:08:31.280
Many countries start seeking replacement

00:08:31.280 --> 00:08:33.930
of traditional fossil energy,

00:08:33.930 --> 00:08:38.850
replacing them with renewable
energy such as solar.

00:08:38.850 --> 00:08:41.971
The coronavirus outbreak
is just the trigger

00:08:41.971 --> 00:08:43.333
of its collapse.

00:08:45.330 --> 00:08:47.860
The founder of homegrown oil-trading firm

00:08:47.860 --> 00:08:51.300
Hin Leong Trading has been
charged with abetment of forgery

00:08:51.300 --> 00:08:53.040
for the purpose of cheating.

00:08:53.040 --> 00:08:55.460
Lim Oon Kuin allegedly asked an employee

00:08:55.460 --> 00:08:59.560
to forge a document to state
that Hin Leong had transferred

00:08:59.560 --> 00:09:02.310
more than 1 million barrels of gas oil

00:09:02.310 --> 00:09:04.730
to China Aviation Oil Corporation.

00:09:04.730 --> 00:09:06.930
This document was allegedly used to secure

00:09:06.930 --> 00:09:10.050
almost $77 million in trade funds

00:09:10.050 --> 00:09:12.200
from a financial institution.

00:09:12.200 --> 00:09:15.930
If found guilty, Lim could
be jailed for up to 10 years

00:09:15.930 --> 00:09:17.520
and fined.

00:09:17.520 --> 00:09:22.220
Hin Leong and Lims is
one of the most secretive

00:09:22.220 --> 00:09:24.210
family businesses in Singapore.

00:09:24.210 --> 00:09:29.210
Multiple attempts to Hin Leong
and Lim's family for comments

00:09:32.570 --> 00:09:34.033
went unsuccessful.

00:09:34.920 --> 00:09:36.910
So after the Hin Leong episode,

00:09:36.910 --> 00:09:40.480
when some banks found themselves
with hundreds of millions

00:09:40.480 --> 00:09:42.390
of dollars of losses,

00:09:42.390 --> 00:09:44.970
we're seeing that the oil industry in Asia

00:09:44.970 --> 00:09:48.630
is going through somewhat of an evolution

00:09:48.630 --> 00:09:51.140
where smaller companies
are finding it harder

00:09:51.140 --> 00:09:53.960
to get credit lines and financing,

00:09:53.960 --> 00:09:57.430
and even bigger companies,
more reputable companies,

00:09:57.430 --> 00:10:00.523
are also finding that credit
lines are being shrunken.

